","E10","E14","E15"]}],"evidenceRequests":["Q3","Q2","Q1"],"summary":"The absenteeism framing is not supported. The 40% rise in occurrences is almost entirely partial-day entries that ShiftLine began recording on 2026-03-30. Full-day absences rose 1.1%. The independent dispatch log shows no change in unstaffed trips, late pull-outs or extraboard use. On-time performance fell on routes with the April recovery cut. Routes with no cut and no construction held at about 82%. Late first-timepoint departures on cut routes show buses arriving just before departure. Construction routes fell further after a second step on 2026-04-20. Early-leave data are confounded by seniority and route length, so the recovery-cut to early-leave link is association only. Restore recovery time, set construction running times, and restate the absence trend. Do not impose discipline or suspend OTP reporting."}}